  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "What is the cardinality of $C\\times D$ for $C={0,1,2,...,11}$ and $D={s,t,u,v}?$",
  "worked_solution": "For any two finite sets $C$ and $D,$ the cardinality of $C\\times D$ is\n\n$$\n|C\\times D|=|C|\\cdot |D|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|C\\times D| & =|C|\\cdot |D| \\\\  & =12\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
